  "notes": "Red label with silver print. 45-R prefix in record number. These labels have “PARLOPHONE” in large stylized letters at the top and the Parlophone £ logo at 3 o’clock with \"Made in Gt. Britain\" directly beneath. The publishing year was printed on the label, as “RECORDING FIRST PUBLISHED 1963″.\n\nMuch like the red label on [m1154826] there are label variations. \nThis version and [r=12975496] have 'MADE IN GT. BRITAIN' printed at 3 o'clock on labels. \n[r=4471796] erroneously omits this designation.\n[r=11764267] and [r=12975526] have 'Made in Gt. Britain' printed on one side but not the other. \n------------------------------------------\nThe red label pressings can be found with MT, MPT and PT tax code, or without.  PT was discontinued shortly before the release of this record.  The early copies typically have PT stamped in the runouts and embossed on the labels, with M subsequent added to give the MPT code.",
